.Dd October 15, 2026
.Dt DS2413GPIO 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ds2413gpio
.Nd Driver for Maxim DS2413 1-Wire GPIO chip
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Cd "ds2413gpio* at onewire?"
.Cd "options DS2413GPIO_EXTRA_FAMILYID 0x55"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver provides a 1-Wire to GPIO bridge with a
.Xr gpio 4
bus at the far end using the DS2413 chip.
.Pp
The DS2413 uses inverted logic for the input and output of the pins.
A 1 read from the pin means that the pin is at logic 0 and a 0 read
means logic 1.
Likewise, writing a 0 to a pin will provide energy to the pin and a 1
will remove energy from the pin.
.Pp
The driver will match the official family ID of the DS2413 chip as well
as the commonly found clone family ID of 0x85.
A kernel can be compiled with DS2413GPIO_EXTRA_FAMILYID to include an
additional family ID that will also match.
.Sh SYSCTL VARIABLES
The following
.Xr sysctl 3
variables are provided:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Li hw.ds2413gpio0.debug
If the driver is compiled with
.Dv DS2413GPIO_DEBUG ,
this node will appear and can be used to set the debugging level.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr gpio 4 ,
.Xr onewire 4 ,
.Xr sysctl 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
driver first appeared in
.Nx 12.0 .
.Sh AUTHORS
.An -nosplit
The
.Nm
driver was written by
.An Brad Spencer Aq Mt brad@anduin.eldar.org .
.Sh BUGS
It is not possible to tell if a pin is literally a input or output pin
as both aspects are active at the same time.
The driver will disallow setting a value on a pin that is set to
GPIO_PIN_INPUT and will report the latched setting on a pin read
instead of the pin value for pins that are set to GPIO_PIN_OUTPUT.
The driver will also set a pin to supply no energy on the pin when it
is set to GPIO_PIN_INPUT.
This should present a situation that is more consistent with
expectations at the cost of not being able to have a pin be both input
and output at the same time.
